  "checkedOn": "2026-10-03",
  "scope": "Completed public scalar reference checks decide Ferraris answer-set membership for one candidate of a finite ground formula theory. Finite typed-refused calls retain their actual reached cause and publish no verdict. Both results use explicit Rust/library contracts and audited extraction/context adaptation. Actual successful Theory::new and owned-vector Interpretation::new calls establish ordered nodes, bounded roots, exact packed storage and retained ownership. Finite generic insertion additionally preserves bounded-prefix writes and first-invalid refusal; unrestricted iterator termination is not claimed. The eventful public checker composes 22 source-checked contexts with imported pure scalar, sequence, iterator and owner operations. Cancellation/deadline reads retain logical object/field identity and consume independent responses; each reservation has its own grant or rejection. Successful runs project to the actual fixed generated checker with the same verdict, statistics and witness; all inner phase contracts are discharged by concrete proofs. Stable is equivalent to answer-set membership, NotModel carries an actual false asserted root, and NonMinimal carries an actual program-owned proper-subset reduct model. Constructed subject checks and consuming accepted-result conversion retain the exact candidate. Public typed refusals recover an actual terminal phase and its reached leaf cause, preserving source order and the returned Stop. Internal loop receipts retain actual reached states and histories, including earlier charged work. No stopped call publishes a decision or establishes exhaustive failure. Stored-reduct construction and public satisfaction queries retain their earlier per-invocation fixed-provider contracts; the runtime event correspondence here covers the public membership checker call graph. Backend failure, divergence and unanswered observations are not typed source returns. There is no unconditional termination/fairness theorem. Source grounding, optimized routes, full solver enumeration, parallel schedules and GPU execution remain outside this milestone.",
